# R3 (SOFT). IMAGE: tp4-stack-1 (exists). D1's exact test sequence on the AUDITS-OFF timed profile c2-packed-tp4-speed (present in the
# image and in the checkout, so the ramp check is valid). Steady prefills here run after four-live packed rounds (the trigger).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over the job file on a throwaway
# commit of tp4/stack-fix (or a descendant) and push the window tag. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. The smoke and its
# check run from the CHECKOUT on the rig host; the server is the IMAGE'S baked tree (--read-only, no bind mount), so C2_IMAGE_TAG picks
# the server and the checkout picks the smoke and the check. THE DRIVER SUBSTITUTES C2_IMAGE_TAG FROM ITS IMAGE_TAG ENV: a chain that
# sets one IMAGE_TAG for all its jobs runs every job on that image, so jobs that need different images are SEPARATE ONE-JOB CHAINS.
# READS: garbage/EOS in concurrent4_steady = the unaudited, timed configuration is affected and the T1/T2 audits are not required for
# the defect; coherent = the audit arm (T1/T2 on, collectives passed to the block, fused commit off) is required, and the two-card
# contrast reduces to audits on or off. The first-prefill ledger line (see G3) is expected on this image, so the run ends red
# whatever the text: a ONE-JOB chain, read by hand. Duration (estimate): 10-13 min (K2, the same profile's smoke: 9.4 min, plus
# concurrent4_steady).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stack-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
